2026-08-02T20:32:23.583646+00:00	Bash	{"command":"/bin/bash -lc '\\"$HORIZON_BIN\\" inbox comment I-1815 --body \\"PROPOSED ROUND-3 UNIT (pre-edit, for C-0072 review). 1. Expose GroupScheme.identityComponentOpens G : G.left.Opens as the public alias of the existing private connected-component carrier, with (identityComponentOpens G).toScheme definitionally (IdentityComponent G).left. 2. Define PicScheme.sectionComponentOpen C (p : 𝟙_ (Over (Spec (.of k))) ⟶ PicScheme C) : (PicScheme C).left.Opens as the image of identityComponentOpens (PicScheme C) under pointTranslation (PicScheme C) (MonObj.one) p. Main intrinsic theorem: ((PicScheme.sectionComponentOpen C p : (PicScheme C).left.Opens) : Set (PicScheme C).left) = connectedComponent (p.left.base default). 3. Package sectionComponentOver C p := Over.mk ((sectionComponentOpen C p).ι ≫ (PicScheme C).hom), an iso Pic0Scheme C ≅ sectionComponentOver C p via the existing Scheme.openImageIsoOver, and a carried IsHQuasiProjectiveWith/FiniteInAffine consequence from an actual Pic0 witness. API comparison: identityComponentCarrier is currently private and only the unit component; pointTranslation/openImageIsoOver are generic automorphism/image adapters; no existing declaration identifies the translated open with the connected component through p or packages that Picard open. Scope limits are explicit: p is a global section, not an arbitrary closed/geometric point; this produces one section-indexed component only, no Pic''^d indexing, degree-shift, cover, arbitrary-field PicEt producer, projectivity, or properness. The carried very-ample result assumes Pic0 IsHQuasiProjectiveWith and is adapter-only; the connected-component equality is the new geometric content. No (rep :) binder or central FGA edit.\\"'"}
